{"id":"n2-184","title":"～折には (〜ori ni wa)","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Expresses 'when' or 'in case of' specific situations or timings.","longExplanation":"The ～折には grammar point is used to emphasize a specific moment or situation (often not very frequent). It can be translated as 'when (the occasion arises)' or 'in case of'.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + 折には, Verb-た form + 折には, い-Adjective + 折には, な-Adjective + な折には, Noun + の折には","examples":[{"jp":"喉が渇く折には、このペットボトルの水を飲んでください。","romaji":"Nodo ga kawaku ori ni wa, kono pettobotoru no mizu o nonde kudasai.","en":"When you get thirsty, please drink water from this bottle.","words":[{"surface":"喉","vocabId":"1600280","reading":"のど"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"渇く","vocabId":"1208520","reading":"かわく"},{"surface":"折","vocabId":"1385780","reading":"おり"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ペットボトル","vocabId":null},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"水","vocabId":"1371260","reading":"みず"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"飲ん","vocabId":"1169870","reading":"のむ","baseForm":"飲む"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[3,4,5]},{"jp":"この地域に来る折には、この神社に必ずお参りしましょう。","romaji":"Kono chiiki ni kuru ori ni wa, kono jinja ni kanarazu omairi shimashou.","en":"When you visit this area, make sure to go to this shrine.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"地域","vocabId":"1420800","reading":"ちいき"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"来る","vocabId":"1547720","reading":"くる"},{"surface":"折","vocabId":"1385780","reading":"おり"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"神社","vocabId":"1364670","reading":"じんじゃ"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"必ず","vocabId":"1487400